__d(function(e,s,i,t,n,o,a){n.exports={version:"2.0",board:"Karnataka State Board / NCERT",grade:7,subject:"Mathematics",textbook:"Mathematics \u2014 Textbook for Class VII",chapter_number:4,chapter_title:"Simple Equations",quiz_type:"MCQ only",mcqs:[{id:"mcq01",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Which of the following is an EQUATION (not just an expression)?",options:["A) 3x + 5","B) 2y \u2212 7 = 11","C) 4a + 2b","D) x\xb2 + 3x"],correct_answer:"B) 2y \u2212 7 = 11",explanation:"An equation has an '=' sign and asserts equality between two expressions. Only option B has an '=' sign. The others are expressions \u2014 they have no equals sign and cannot be solved."},{id:"mcq02",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Solve: x + 9 = 17",options:["A) x = 26","B) x = 8","C) x = 7","D) x = 9"],correct_answer:"B) x = 8",explanation:"Transpose 9 to RHS: x = 17 \u2212 9 = 8. Verify: 8 + 9 = 17 \u2713."},{id:"mcq03",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Solve: 4x = 36",options:["A) x = 32","B) x = 40","C) x = 9","D) x = 144"],correct_answer:"C) x = 9",explanation:"Divide both sides by 4: x = 36/4 = 9. Verify: 4 \xd7 9 = 36 \u2713."},{id:"mcq04",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Solve: 2x \u2212 3 = 11",options:["A) x = 4","B) x = 7","C) x = 8","D) x = 5"],correct_answer:"B) x = 7",explanation:"Transpose \u22123: 2x = 11 + 3 = 14. Divide by 2: x = 7. Verify: 2(7) \u2212 3 = 14 \u2212 3 = 11 \u2713."},{id:"mcq05",difficulty:"Easy",question:"What is the solution of: x/4 = 6?",options:["A) x = 2","B) x = 10","C) x = 24","D) x = 3/2"],correct_answer:"C) x = 24",explanation:"Multiply both sides by 4: x = 6 \xd7 4 = 24. Verify: 24/4 = 6 \u2713."},{id:"mcq06",difficulty:"Easy",question:"In the equation 5x + 3 = 18, the LHS is:",options:["A) 5x","B) 18","C) 5x + 3","D) 3"],correct_answer:"C) 5x + 3",explanation:"LHS = Left Hand Side = the entire expression to the LEFT of the '=' sign = 5x + 3. RHS = 18."},{id:"mcq07",difficulty:"Easy",question:"A number increased by 14 gives 30. The equation is:",options:["A) x \u2212 14 = 30","B) 14x = 30","C) x + 14 = 30","D) x/14 = 30"],correct_answer:"C) x + 14 = 30",explanation:"'A number increased by 14' = x + 14. 'Gives 30' = = 30. So equation is x + 14 = 30, giving x = 16."},{id:"mcq08",difficulty:"Easy",question:"If 3x + 5 = 20, what is the value of x?",options:["A) 3","B) 5","C) 8","D) 7"],correct_answer:"B) 5",explanation:"3x = 20 \u2212 5 = 15. x = 15/3 = 5. Verify: 3(5) + 5 = 15 + 5 = 20 \u2713."},{id:"mcq09",difficulty:"Easy",question:"When you transpose a term from LHS to RHS, its sign:",options:["A) stays the same","B) changes to zero","C) doubles","D) changes (+ becomes \u2212, \xd7 becomes \xf7)"],correct_answer:"D) changes (+ becomes \u2212, \xd7 becomes \xf7)",explanation:"Transposing means moving a term to the other side of the equation \u2014 its sign must change. Addition becomes subtraction, multiplication becomes division, and vice versa. This is the shortcut equivalent of performing the inverse operation on both sides."},{id:"mcq10",difficulty:"Easy",question:"Verify: Is x = 3 the solution of 5x \u2212 6 = 9?",options:["A) Yes, because 5(3)\u22126 = 9","B) No, because 5(3)\u22126 = 6","C) Yes, because 5(3) = 15","D) No, because 5(3)\u22126 = 12"],correct_answer:"A) Yes, because 5(3)\u22126 = 9",explanation:"Substitute x=3: LHS = 5(3) \u2212 6 = 15 \u2212 6 = 9 = RHS. So x=3 IS the solution. Verification confirms correctness by substituting the value and checking LHS = RHS."},{id:"mcq11",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"Solve: 3x + 7 = x + 19",options:["A) x = 4","B) x = 6","C) x = 8","D) x = 3"],correct_answer:"B) x = 6",explanation:"Transpose x to LHS and 7 to RHS: 3x \u2212 x = 19 \u2212 7 \u2192 2x = 12 \u2192 x = 6. Verify: LHS = 3(6)+7 = 25. RHS = 6+19 = 25 \u2713."},{id:"mcq12",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"Solve: 5(x \u2212 2) = 3(x + 4)",options:["A) x = 7","B) x = 11","C) x = 9","D) x = 5"],correct_answer:"B) x = 11",explanation:"Expand: 5x \u2212 10 = 3x + 12. Transpose: 5x \u2212 3x = 12 + 10 \u2192 2x = 22 \u2192 x = 11. Verify: LHS = 5(9) = 45. RHS = 3(15) = 45 \u2713."},{id:"mcq13",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"The sum of two consecutive even numbers is 50. The smaller number is:",options:["A) 22","B) 24","C) 26","D) 20"],correct_answer:"B) 24",explanation:"Let the even numbers be n and n+2. n + (n+2) = 50 \u2192 2n + 2 = 50 \u2192 2n = 48 \u2192 n = 24. Smaller number = 24. The numbers are 24 and 26. Check: 24+26 = 50 \u2713."},{id:"mcq14",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"A father is 4 times his son's age. If the sum of their ages is 60, the son's age is:",options:["A) 10","B) 12","C) 15","D) 20"],correct_answer:"B) 12",explanation:"Let son's age = x. Father = 4x. Sum: x + 4x = 60 \u2192 5x = 60 \u2192 x = 12. Son = 12, Father = 48. Verify: 12 + 48 = 60 \u2713."},{id:"mcq15",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"Solve: (2x + 1)/3 = 5",options:["A) x = 7","B) x = 8","C) x = 6","D) x = 14"],correct_answer:"A) x = 7",explanation:"Multiply both sides by 3: 2x + 1 = 15. Transpose 1: 2x = 14. x = 7. Verify: (2\xd77+1)/3 = 15/3 = 5 \u2713."},{id:"mcq16",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"The perimeter of a square is 52 cm. The equation for its side (s) is:",options:["A) s + 4 = 52","B) 4s = 52","C) s\xb2 = 52","D) s/4 = 52"],correct_answer:"B) 4s = 52",explanation:"Perimeter of square = 4 \xd7 side = 4s. Equation: 4s = 52. Solving: s = 13 cm. Verify: 4 \xd7 13 = 52 \u2713."},{id:"mcq17",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"A number is multiplied by 6 and then 8 is subtracted. The result is 40. The number is:",options:["A) 6","B) 8","C) 12","D) 10"],correct_answer:"B) 8",explanation:"Equation: 6x \u2212 8 = 40 \u2192 6x = 48 \u2192 x = 8. Verify: 6(8) \u2212 8 = 48 \u2212 8 = 40 \u2713."},{id:"mcq18",difficulty:"Moderate",question:"If 4 is subtracted from twice a number, the result is 10. Twice the number is:",options:["A) 14","B) 7","C) 6","D) 3"],correct_answer:"A) 14",explanation:"Equation: 2x \u2212 4 = 10 \u2192 2x = 14. So 'twice the number' = 2x = 14 (and x = 7). The question asks for 2x, not x."},{id:"mcq19",difficulty:"Advanced",question:"The difference between two numbers is 8. If the larger is 3 times the smaller, the smaller number is:",options:["A) 2","B) 4","C) 6","D) 8"],correct_answer:"B) 4",explanation:"Let smaller = x. Larger = 3x. Difference: 3x \u2212 x = 8 \u2192 2x = 8 \u2192 x = 4. Smaller = 4, Larger = 12. Verify: 12 \u2212 4 = 8 \u2713 and 12 = 3\xd74 \u2713."},{id:"mcq20",difficulty:"Advanced",question:"Present ages: Asha is 5 years older than Meena. 10 years ago, Asha was twice Meena's age. Asha's present age is:",options:["A) 15","B) 20","C) 10","D) 25"],correct_answer:"A) 15",explanation:"Let Meena's age = x. Asha's age = x + 5. 10 years ago: Meena = x\u221210, Asha = x+5\u221210 = x\u22125. Condition: x\u22125 = 2(x\u221210) \u2192 x\u22125 = 2x\u221220 \u2192 20\u22125 = 2x\u2212x \u2192 x = 15 (Meena). Asha = 15+5 = 20. Wait \u2014 recheck: x=15 is Meena, Asha=20. Verify: 10 years ago Meena=5, Asha=10. Is 10=2\xd75? \u2713. Answer: Asha's present age = 20. Select B."}]}},2773,[]);